Top-K design (example Top-K search/ Top-K video on yt)


Event publisher would send input to a kafka stream which is partitioned by videoId.

When we say partitioned by videoId is we will have different partitions for each video and those each would have a consumer for them

for example say we have a 1000 partitions than we would do this.

partition = hash(videoId) % NUM_PARTITIONS

This ensures same videoId always goes to same partition. 

So each partition can calculate its top-k and we can aggregate all to calculate global top-k. {done using heaps}

This aggregation we can use Apache Flink or Apache Spark streaming etc.

We convert this aggregation to parquet files (its a format optimised for analytics has compression/columnor search) and store in S3.

example parquet file (storing things together not rowwise which forces whole read to get to one property,)

Column "videoId": [abc123, def456, ghi789]
Column "views":   [1500, 3200, 875]
Column "duration":[120, 95, 60]


We can also than put a dump of this in some time series db (Promethus/TimescaleDB) to quickly get results and historical or low severity ones could be found from S3